      "rationale": "The bug is in group_functions() (sqlparse/engine/grouping.py): it detects CREATE and TABLE keywords case-insensitively via .upper(), but checks for the AS keyword with an exact `tmp_token.value == 'AS'`, so a lower/mixed-case \"as\" is missed. This makes the function wrongly believe a \"CREATE TABLE ... AS SELECT ...\" statement has no AS clause and skip grouping function calls in the SELECT part entirely - reproducing the reported \"grouping function\" regression (assert False on the grouping check). The test asserts that CREATE TABLE ... AS SELECT bar(x) ... groups bar(x) into sql.Function regardless of the AS keyword's casing (matching the already-correct upper-case behavior), while also confirming untouched correct behaviors (plain CREATE TABLE definitions not being grouped as functions, and ordinary function calls) continue to work.",
